omponents/dashboard-command-palette.tsx (grep only)", "components/dashboard-header.tsx (grep only)", "components/icons/github-icon.tsx (grep only)", "components/intel-dashboard.tsx (grep only)", "components/issue-viewer.tsx (grep only)", "components/landing-auth-buttons.tsx (grep only)", "components/landing-hero-media.tsx (grep only)", "components/landing-theme-toggle.tsx (grep only)", "components/proactive-alerts.tsx (grep only)", "components/providers/user-provider.tsx (grep only)", "components/recently-viewed-dashboard.tsx (grep only)", "components/repo-card.tsx (grep only)", "components/repo-command-palette.tsx (grep only)", "components/repo-contributions-page.tsx (grep only)", "components/repo-detail-page.tsx (grep only)", "components/repo-detail-panel.tsx (grep only)", "components/repo-grid.tsx (grep only)", "components/repo-health-badges.tsx (grep only)", "components/repo-intel-page.tsx (grep only)", "components/repo-intel-tab.tsx (grep only)", "components/repo-list.tsx (grep only)", "components/search-hero.tsx (grep only)", "components/search-page.tsx (grep only)", "components/search-personalized-section.tsx (grep only)", "components/search-pipeline-timeline.tsx (grep only)", "components/search-result-card.tsx (grep only)", "components/search-saved-section.tsx (grep only)", "components/search-trending-strip.tsx (grep only)", "components/settings-page.tsx (grep only)", "components/star-note-toast.tsx (grep only)", "components/theme-provider.tsx (grep only)", "components/token-expired-banner.tsx (grep only)", "components/trending-dashboard.tsx (grep only)", "components/trending-empty-state.tsx (grep only)", "components/trending-section.tsx (grep only)", "components/use-command-palette-shortcut.ts (grep only)", "components/user-menu.tsx (grep only)", "app/(authenticated)/contribute/page.tsx (grep only)", "app/(authenticated)/dashboard/page.tsx (grep only)", "app/(authenticated)/intel/page.tsx (grep only)", "app/(authenticated)/recently-viewed/page.tsx (grep only)", "app/(authenticated)/repo/[owner]/[repo]/contributions/page.tsx (grep only)", "app/(authenticated)/repo/[owner]/[repo]/page.tsx (grep only)", "app/(authenticated)/search/page.tsx (grep only)", "app/(authenticated)/settings/page.tsx (grep only)", "app/(authenticated)/trending/page.tsx (grep only)", "app/auth/error/page.tsx (grep only)", "app/global-error.tsx (grep only)", "app/layout.tsx (grep only)", "hooks/use-mobile.ts (grep only)", "hooks/use-toast.ts (grep only)"], "note": "scripts/ and docker/migrations/ hold identical migration copies, so migration labels cite scripts/ only. UI components were covered by targeted grep, not read line by line. No ai_browser_call found. All model calls run in Next.js API routes. The bring-your-own key goes from the browser to the app's own server in a header. RLS is on for every user table, and composite owner foreign keys block cross-user tag and collection links. Cron and test-observability routes check CRON_SECRET. README and issue markdown render through react-markdown without raw HTML. No committed secrets. Both env examples hold placeholders only.", "labels": [{"category": "database_rules", "file": "supabase/migrations/20260421183257_remote_schema.sql", "line_start": 580, "line_end": 580, "related_file": "lib/ai-weekly-limit.ts", "related_line": 47, "what": "profiles_update_own lets each user update every column of their own profiles row with the public anon key (GRANT ALL at line 868). All AI quota state lives there (ai_brief_count, ai_intel_count, ai_search_count, last_ai_categorization_at, last_personalized_search_at, last_contribution_scan_at, single_repo_scan_day_count), so a user can reset their counters and bypass the paid AI limits", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "high"}, {"category": "database_rules", "file": "scripts/019_ai_limits_atomic.sql", "line_start": 10, "line_end": 20, "related_file": "supabase/migrations/20260421183257_remote_schema.sql", "related_line": 932, "what": "check_and_increment_ai_limit is SECURITY DEFINER and takes the user id and the limits as caller arguments. There is no REVOKE, and default privileges grant functions to anon, so anyone with the public key can call it for any user id and burn that user's AI quota", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "medium"}, {"category": "database_rules", "file": "supabase/migrations/20260421183257_remote_schema.sql", "line_start": 84, "line_end": 150, "related_file": "supabase/migrations/20260421183257_remote_schema.sql", "related_line": 822, "what": "get_valid_token and token_needs_refresh are SECURITY DEFINER with no search_path, granted to anon, and take any user id. They returned a user's GitHub token. Migration 014 drops them, but the live schema snapshot still has them. They now point at a dropped column, so they fail today", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "throwaway", "confidence": "low"}, {"category": "database_rules", "file": "lib/user-metadata.ts", "line_start": 239, "line_end": 245, "related_file": "components/settings-page.tsx", "related_line": 476, "what": "The 200-tag and 50-collection per-user caps (also lines 385-391) run in browser code against the anon client. RLS allows the inserts, and no database rule enforces the caps, so a user can create unlimited rows directly", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "low"}, {"category": "note_public_key", "file": "lib/supabase/client.ts", "line_start": 5, "line_end": 6, "what": "NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY used in the browser client. Public by design", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "keep", "confidence": "high"}, {"category": "ai_prompt_only_rule", "file": "app/api/search/repos/route.ts", "line_start": 379, "line_end": 379, "related_file": "app/api/search/repos/route.ts", "related_line": 87, "what": "Prompt says generate 3-5 GitHub search queries. The schema only sets min(1) with no max, and lines 418-425 run every returned query against GitHub in parallel with the user's token", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "medium"}, {"category": "ai_prompt_only_rule", "file": "app/api/search/personalized/route.ts", "line_start": 105, "line_end": 105, "related_file": "app/api/search/personalized/route.ts", "related_line": 28, "what": "Prompt says identify 2-4 themes. The themes array has no max, and lines 121-123 run one GitHub search per theme", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "medium"}, {"category": "ai_prompt_only_rule", "file": "lib/ai-categorize.ts", "line_start": 122, "line_end": 123, "related_file": "lib/ai-categorize.ts", "related_line": 47, "what": "Prompt asks for 5-12 collections and 15-25 tags. TaxonomySchema has no array bounds, and lines 136-143 accept whatever count the model returns", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "medium"}, {"category": "ai_prompt_only_rule", "file": "lib/ai-categorize.ts", "line_start": 176, "line_end": 177, "related_file": "lib/ai-categorize.ts", "related_line": 186, "what": "Prompt says 1-3 collections and 1-3 tags per repo. Code filters to the known vocabulary but never caps the count", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "low"}, {"category": "ai_prompt_only_rule", "file": "app/api/search/repos/route.ts", "line_start": 593, "line_end": 593, "related_file": "app/api/search/repos/route.ts", "related_line": 120, "what": "Prompt and schema text ask for exactly 3 evidence bullets of at most 60 characters. The schema has no length or count limit and the code does not trim", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "low"}, {"category": "ai_no_human_review", "file": "app/api/ai/repo-intel/route.ts", "line_start": 156, "line_end": 185, "what": "Model output is written straight into the global repo_insights cache that every user reads for 7 days, with no review", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "medium"}, {"category": "ai_no_human_review", "file": "app/api/ai/categorize/route.ts", "line_start": 316, "line_end": 411, "what": "AI-made tags, collections and assignments are written to the user's data right after one click, with no preview or confirm step", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "low"}, {"category": "fake_action", "file": "components/search-star-popover.tsx", "line_start": 26, "line_end": 49, "related_file": "app/api/github/star/route.ts", "related_line": 48, "what": "Star button never checks response.ok, so it shows Starred even when the API returns 401, 429 or 500. The tags and collections picked in the popover are never saved (see next label)", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "high"}, {"category": "fake_action", "file": "app/api/github/star/route.ts", "line_start": 45, "line_end": 83, "what": "Tag and collection assignment looks up user_starred_repos by github_repo_id, a column that table does not have. The lookup errors, the error is ignored, nothing is written, and the route still returns success", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "high"}, {"category": "fake_action", "file": "app/api/github/star/route.ts", "line_start": 139, "line_end": 162, "what": "Unstar cleanup uses the same missing github_repo_id column, so local rows, tags and collections are not deleted while the route returns success. The next full sync removes them later", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "medium"}, {"category": "mock_data", "file": "lib/mock-data.ts", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 427, "what": "Sample tags, collections and repos (next.js, supabase and others) with fixed star counts. Not imported anywhere", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "throwaway", "confidence": "low"}, {"category": "mock_data", "file": "app/page.tsx", "line_start": 244, "line_end": 266, "related_file": "app/page.tsx", "related_line": 424, "what": "Landing page snapshots use hardcoded repos, star counts and contribution issues with fixed scores as product illustrations", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "keep", "confidence": "low"}, {"category": "security_other", "file": "lib/tokens.ts", "line_start": 89, "line_end": 99, "related_file": "docs/security-hardening-plan.md", "related_line": 28, "what": "GitHub OAuth access and refresh tokens are stored as plain text in github_oauth_tokens. The repo's own hardening plan says to encrypt them before launch", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "medium"}, {"category": "security_other", "file": "lib/use-ai-key.ts", "line_start": 55, "line_end": 72, "what": "The user's own OpenAI, Anthropic or OpenRouter key is stored in plain localStorage and sent as the x-ai-key header on every AI call, readable by any script on the page", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "medium"}, {"category": "security_other", "file": "app/api/ai/repo-intel/route.ts", "line_start": 154, "line_end": 185, "related_file": "lib/ai-repo-intel.ts", "related_line": 78, "what": "Issue titles that anyone can write on GitHub go into the prompt unguarded, and the summary is cached for all users. Any user can force a rewrite with refresh=true, and with their own key no quota applies", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "medium"}, {"category": "security_other", "file": "lib/rate-limit.ts", "line_start": 14, "line_end": 14, "related_file": "app/api/github/star/route.ts", "related_line": 24, "what": "Star, readme and issue rate limits use an in-memory Map. On Vercel each instance counts separately, so the limits are not global", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "low"}, {"category": "security_other", "file": "lib/ai-weekly-limit.ts", "line_start": 77, "line_end": 106, "related_file": "app/api/github/contribution-opportunities/route.ts", "related_line": 94, "what": "Personalized-search cooldown and the single-repo scan cap read then write with no lock, so parallel requests can pass the limit", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "low"}, {"category": "security_other", "file": "modules/auth/lib/client.ts", "line_start": 13, "line_end": 13, "related_file": "app/auth/login/page.tsx", "related_line": 29, "what": "OAuth asks for read:org and notifications, which no code uses, plus public_repo write access. The repo's hardening plan says to narrow scopes", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "low"}, {"category": "security_other", "file": "app/api/search/repos/route.ts", "line_start": 381, "line_end": 381, "related_file": "app/api/search/repos/route.ts", "related_line": 531, "what": "Raw user query is pasted into three prompts with no guard. Impact is limited to that user's own search", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "keep", "confidence": "low"}, {"category": "security_other", "file": "app/api/github/health/route.ts", "line_start": 51, "line_end": 58, "related_file": "app/api/github/health/route.ts", "related_line": 208, "what": "repoIds has no size cap and the route makes one sequential GitHub release call per starred repo, with no rate limit", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "low"}, {"category": "security_other", "file": "docker-compose.yml", "line_start": 22, "line_end": 22, "what": "Docker socket mounted into the ofelia cron container. Read-only still gives full Docker API access", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "low"}, {"category": "hardcoded_config", "file": "app/api/ai/categorize/route.ts", "line_start": 20, "line_end": 20, "related_file": "README.md", "related_line": 101, "what": "Categorization cooldown is 7 days in code. README says 24 hours, AGENTS.md line 115 says 24h, and migration 010 is named daily limit", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "medium"}, {"category": "hardcoded_config", "file": "lib/search-cache.ts", "line_start": 6, "line_end": 6, "related_file": "README.md", "related_line": 119, "what": "Discover cache TTL is 7 days in code and in migration 016. README says 30-day cache", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "keep", "confidence": "low"}, {"category": "hardcoded_config", "file": "lib/ai-weekly-limit.ts", "line_start": 14, "line_end": 18, "related_file": "scripts/012_ai_weekly_limits.sql", "related_line": 1, "what": "AI quotas hardcoded in code (brief 20 per week). Migration 012 comments say 10 per week for brief and intel, two values for the same limit", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "keep", "confidence": "low"}, {"category": "hardcoded_config", "file": "lib/ai-provider.ts", "line_start": 8, "line_end": 12, "what": "Model ids hardcoded per provider (gemini-2.0-flash-001, gpt-4o-mini, claude-haiku-4-5)", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "keep", "confidence": "low"}, {"category": "hardcoded_config", "file": "sentry.client.config.ts", "line_start": 5, "line_end": 5, "related_file": "sentry.server.config.ts", "related_line": 6, "what": "tracesSampleRate fixed at 1.0 in all three Sentry configs", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "keep", "confidence": "low"}, {"category": "hardcoded_config", "file": "docker/ofelia.ini", "line_start": 3, "line_end": 4, "what": "Cron job hardcodes container name stardash-app-1 and http://localhost:3000", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "keep", "confidence": "low"}, {"category": "hardcoded_config", "file": "next.config.mjs", "line_start": 7, "line_end": 7, "what": "ignoreBuildErrors true, so type errors never fail a production build", "keep_rewrite_throwaway": "rewrite", "confidence": "low"}]}